      "reaches the long table for about forty minutes in August and then",
      "gives it up for the rest of the day.",
      "",
      "Three things I want to keep hold of this week:",
      "",
      "  - finish the reading notes before starting anything new",
      "  - walk the loop past the reservoir at least twice",
      "  - call Ines back, properly, not a message",
      "",
      "The tomatoes on the sill have gone leggy from reaching. I keep",
      "meaning to turn the tray a quarter every morning and I keep",
      "forgetting until the stems have already decided.",
      "",
      "Later --",
      "",
      "Walked to the market for coffee and came back with coffee, two",
      "heads of fennel and a chipped enamel jug I did not need and could",
      "not leave. The woman selling it said it had been her mother's and",
      "then, seeing my face, said that about everything on the table.",
      "",
      "Read forty pages standing up because sitting down would have meant",
      "admitting the afternoon was over.",
      "",
      "Things I noticed and want to write about properly some other time: the way the light comes off the wet road after the sprinklers run at four; how nobody in this neighbourhood says goodbye on the phone, they just stop; the two cats on Ellery Street who have divided the block along a line only they can see.",
      "",
      "Tomorrow --",
      "",
      "  - the fennel, before it goes soft",
      "  - the reading notes, first thing, before anything else opens",
      "  - ring the letting agent about the window that will not close",
